{"id": "EUVD-2026-25453", "enisaUuid": "a0c7d329-420c-35bc-a0f8-bb24604a930f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: spi-dw-dma: fix print error log when wait finish transaction\n\nIf an error occurs, the device may not have a current message. In this\ncase, the system will crash.\n\nIn this case, it's better to use dev from the struct ctlr (struct spi_controller*).", "datePublished": "2026-04-24T14:35:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bac13309339b6f1ac02e6e53ebc75cf61483c396", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8188ff3cfaa5621212b08473488cdbe41f86531", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aae4a47073b12c23eb1d2c5401bda442fbe27bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/184f5aaf72f1f1c73e66bae0b8d28e81c2f2a72f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b46d61890632c8f8b117147b6923bff4b42ccb7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x9pc-8g9f-68mf", "CVE-2026-31560"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0be09851-2bca-3569-b24a-f774c7a57f9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bdbdf0f06337d3661b64c0288c291cb06624065e <b8188ff3cfaa5621212b08473488cdbe41f86531"}, {"id": "28d0eb40-fe3f-3e43-b40f-5f9b495c8ff1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.11"}, {"id": "3f39ddf3-7aab-3526-a86e-197d6ad863ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "53d59d12-9dd2-3e83-95d4-fadc4bc1472a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bdbdf0f06337d3661b64c0288c291cb06624065e <184f5aaf72f1f1c73e66bae0b8d28e81c2f2a72f"}, {"id": "55a28692-654c-3a9b-9d28-1dfb9b2df2f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bdbdf0f06337d3661b64c0288c291cb06624065e <bac13309339b6f1ac02e6e53ebc75cf61483c396"}, {"id": "59f41c06-d614-3cc3-9ef7-5723694b9da0", "product